<section class="story section shell" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
  <div class="section-heading story__heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">About Brett</p>
    <h2 id="about-title">A creative practice built on expression, experimentation and joy.</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="story__grid">
    <article class="story-card story-card--feature">
      <span class="story-card__number">01</span>
      <h3>The artist</h3>
      <p>
        Brett is a self-taught artist based in Donnybrook, Western Australia. His work is grounded in a genuine
        fascination with the way fluid paint travels, combines and creates forms that cannot be repeated.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="story-card">
      <span class="story-card__number">02</span>
      <h3>The journey</h3>
      <p>
        He discovered paint pouring during a pivotal period in his life while receiving support for mental health
        challenges. A new creative outlet quickly became a powerful and deeply resonant form of expression.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="story-card" id="studio">
      <span class="story-card__number">03</span>
      <h3>The studio</h3>
      <p>
        Now fully recovered and retired, Brett spends his time refining his technique in a converted shed-studio on
        his rural property, surrounded by the landscape of South West Western Australia.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="story-card story-card--accent">
      <span class="story-card__number">04</span>
      <h3>The artwork</h3>
      <p>
        Every piece is unique—driven by colour, movement and the freedom of the medium. The finished work preserves a
        moment of controlled experimentation that can never be recreated in exactly the same way.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
